   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "1If severe penicillin allergy (previous angioedema, anaphylaxis or urticaria), discuss with doctor. 2Avoid ibuprofen if peptic ulcer, asthma, hypertension, heart failure, kidney disease or pregnant. 3Test for malaria with rapid diagnostic test if available. If not available send blood to laboratory for microscopy. Rapid tests may stay positive for up to one month after successful treatment. A negative test does not exclude malaria, request a second test. 4Notify within 24 hours via NMC App (download from NICD website/app store) or www.nicd.ac.za/nmc-overview/notification-process.",
